
### SCALING: increase replicas from 2 to 4
$ kubectl scale deployment/lab2-app --replicas=4
deployment.apps/lab2-app scaled
$ kubectl get pods -l app=lab2-app
NAME                        READY   STATUS        RESTARTS   AGE
lab2-app-56dd487c9b-2ctj2   1/1     Terminating   0          73s
lab2-app-56dd487c9b-682tp   1/1     Terminating   0          86s
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-bv4qd    1/1     Running       0          26s
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-snrr5    1/1     Running       0          38s
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-tnb9c    1/1     Running       0          12s
lab2-app-88f4c9fc9-v8vv5    1/1     Running       0          12s

$ kubectl get deployment lab2-app
NAME       READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
lab2-app   4/4     4            4           19m

### scale back down to 2
$ kubectl scale deployment/lab2-app --replicas=2
deployment.apps/lab2-app scaled
